Wasmer 7.3.0 is built from the pinned tag in named variants. Each variant's
patches.list gives its ordered patch sets. wasmer/build.nix builds the CLIs
through Nix; make wasmer-<variant> links one at work/wasmer/<variant>.
Every variant builds only the Cranelift compiler backend; ServiceCache does
not build Wasmer's BUSL-1.1-licensed Singlepass and LLVM backends.

- stock: no patches. A guest with no extension declaration must run under
  it unchanged, and it is the unpatched baseline for the other variants.

- fixes: fixes to upstream Wasmer that are not specific to ServiceCache.

- extensions: the import namespaces a guest can opt into — currently
  ictrobot_shm_v1, cross-instance shared memory — with none of the host
  machinery. It applies the fixes set and then every extension's set, so
  an extension guest runs standalone, needing nothing from the servicecache
  set. Each extension lives whole in extensions/<name>/ at the repository root:
  its specification, guest header, demo, smoke test and its own patch set.
  A package that declares extensions builds and smoke-tests under this CLI.

- jitdump: perf profiling of generated code. It applies the fixes and
  extensions sets and then its own, which registers an engine's code with
  perf, as a perf map or a jitdump with unwind information, also in a
  forked child. It is off unless selected; the CLI takes --profiler jitdump.

- servicecache: the runtime the host embeds ([patch.crates-io] in Cargo.toml
  points at its separate host checkout). It applies the fixes, extensions and
  jitdump sets and then its own, which makes a guest coroutine suspend on a
  blocking host wait instead of parking its OS thread, lets guest threads be
  resurrected on fresh threads in a forked child, rebuilds the selector after
  a fork, replaces a clone's listening socket, snapshots shared memory across
  the native fork so clones diverge, keeps host I/O from going through a
  runtime handle captured at construction, and waits on a guest futex or on a
  socket's host descriptor in the kernel. Suspension is off unless the host
  enables it; the I/O changes apply always.

The flake exposes wasmer-<variant> and wasmer-<variant>-tests packages. The
matching make targets link the CLI or run its unit tests. Smoke tests build
the CLI they need; guest builds do not. Upstream's integration suites and the
backends we do not build are left to upstream's CI. Two upstream tests that
download from the public registry are skipped in Nix's network-isolated sandbox.

make setup-wasmer prepares work/src/wasmer/servicecache for host Cargo,
without Nix. make build and make test use this checkout. It is separate from
the immutable Nix source used for the servicecache CLI.

The patch sets are developed as stacked branches of a checkout under
work/wasmer-dev — a set's branch contains the branches below it — and
written back with export-patches.sh, which maintains each patch's
Last-Update date; make lint checks it against Git history. The sets are
maintained for the sys backend on Linux. setup-dev.sh (make
setup-wasmer-dev) clones that checkout when it is missing and rebuilds
any of those branches whose export no longer reproduces its committed
set, and the branches stacked on it, from the committed series; every
other branch is left alone.
